Task: Fix the classification vocabulary mismatch (Phase 2, Tier 1)
Track: fy_tax_pack_20260729
INSERTED TASK - not in the original plan. Found while determining how to
identify capital works expenses for the migration 057 backfill, which
cannot be written without deciding this mapping.

THE DEFECT
Two Postgres enums describe the same concepts with different labels:
  renovations.classification      repair | capital_improvement | initial_repair
  expenses.manual_classification  Repair | Capital Works       | Immediate Repair

tax-report/page.tsx did:
  const effective = expense.manual_classification ?? renovation.classification;
  if (effective === "Capital Works")        -> capitalImprovements
  else if (effective === "Immediate Repair") -> initialRepairs
  else                                       -> repairs

manual_classification is an OPTIONAL override, null for most expenses. The
inherited renovation value was therefore compared against labels it could
never equal, and fell through to the else branch every time.

MEASURED IMPACT (executed before/after, no manual override):
  case                             OLD                        NEW
  capital improvement              repairs / DEDUCTED NOW  -> capitalImprovements / cost base
  initial repair                   repairs / DEDUCTED NOW  -> initialRepairs / cost base
  repair                           repairs / DEDUCTED NOW  -> repairs / DEDUCTED NOW

All three collapsed into the current-year deduction bucket. Only a plain
repair was correct, and only by coincidence. Consequence: current-year
deductions overstated, CGT cost base understated - erring in the
taxpayer's favour, the direction that attracts ATO scrutiny.

Severity note: this affects the FY2025-26 report the user intends to send
to their tax agent, so it was fixed immediately rather than deferred to
Phase 4 where classification routing was already scheduled.

NAMING TRAP DOCUMENTED
"Immediate Repair" does NOT mean immediately deductible. It denotes an
initial repair at purchase - work to bring a property to rentable
condition - which is capital and belongs in the CGT cost base. Confirmed
against the report itself: the initialRepairs group renders as "Initial
Repairs at Purchase ... Not immediately deductible - added to the CGT cost
base", and initialRepairTotal feeds costBase in tax-report-pdf.tsx:426.
isDeductibleNow() encodes this so callers never reason from the label.

A THIRD vocabulary exists on the AI path (AiTaxClassification: "Immediate
Deduction" | "Capital Works (Div 43)" | "Plant & Equipment (Div 40)"). It
is deliberately out of scope here - the report reads only the manual and
renovation columns - but Phase 4 should confirm whether the schedule needs
to consume it.

